<!--META-DATA
{
	tags: for,
}
-->

<statement>
<p>
	This function will identify which letter on the game keyboard is associated with the coordinates of the (valid) point provided.
</p>

<tabular valign="top" top="minor">
	<col width="12%"/>
	<col width="88%"/>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell>Inputs:</cell>
		<cell>
			<p><pf>x</pf> (double) double — is the x-coordinate of the point</p>
			<p><pf>y</pf> (double) double — is the y-coordinate of the point</p>
			<p><pf>keyboard</pf> (struct) number — is a structure containing 26 fields (one for each letter); each of the letters contains a struct with three fields--described in detail previously</p>
		</cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell>Outputs:</cell>
		<cell>
			<p><pf>letter</pf> (character) number — is the (uppercase) letter on the keyboard box that contains the point</p>
		</cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell>Details:</cell>
		<cell><p>Note that we are considering the following keyboard.</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>However,</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>there is no plot/game board involved in this function</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>. The inputs are numbers and the output is a letter.</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>Hint: compare the provided</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>x</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>and</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>y</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>to the</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>xvals</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>and</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>yvals</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>stored in the</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>keyboard</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>structure</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>NOTE: The</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>keyboard</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>input below must be provided. You can call your</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>HW7P1</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>or use one of the keyboard variables provided in</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>this .mat</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>file. The colors on the keyboard don't matter, you just need the x and y values.</p></cell>
	</row>
</tabular>

<p>
	Examples:
<program>
	<code>
		INPUTS
		2.5, 4.8, keyboard
		OUTPUT
		'W'
		INPUTS
		12.15, 1.43, keyboard
		OUTPUT
		'B'
	</code>
</program>
</p>
</statement>
